From 3cded9eef308acc47288eb0834f4dc464c045ca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade Next.js to 16.3.1 and postcss to 8.5.26

Vercel flagged next@15.1.6 as a vulnerable version on deploy. The patched
15.x line (15.5.23) clears the Next advisories but leaves high-severity ones
in bundled postcss and sharp that only resolve on 16.x, so this goes to 16.

React 19 satisfies the new peer range unchanged, and nothing in the app used
an API that moved: route handlers already awaited their params.

npm audit now reports 0 vulnerabilities. Verified on 16.3.1: build passes,
e2e 12/12, e2e:mobile 7/7, no console errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018JjAD7WNZmP26cnkvFDZws
